  "hints": [
    "Start from a single-server hash table. What breaks first as data and traffic grow?",
    "Partition with consistent hashing (with virtual nodes) and replicate each key to the next N nodes on the ring. How do W and R relate to N?",
    "Cover quorum (W + R > N), vector clocks for conflicts, sloppy quorum with hinted handoff for temporary failures, Merkle-tree anti-entropy for permanent ones, gossip for membership, and the write path (commit log, memtable, SSTables)."
  ],
  "level": "Beginner",
  "nonFunctionalReqs": [
    "Scales horizontally to hundreds of nodes",
